    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with a calculated offensive focus on high-upside matchups against favorable arms. **Seiya Suzuki** (66.29) and **Tyler Soderstrom** (66.15) anchor our lineup, benefiting from optimal #4 spots and exploitable matchups against Springs and Rea, respectively. **Austin Riley** (62.90) is our premier leverage play; while he faces an elite holding pitcher, his historical BvP edge (35 PA) and favorable park factors allow him to transcend the defensive risk. Despite the daunting presence of Ohtani on the mound, **Corbin Carroll** (60.19) remains a mandatory start; his elite sprint speed and #2 lineup positioning provide the necessary stolen base floor that keeps him in the starting nine despite the poor SP_xERA environment.\n\nThe final roster spot was a tight contest between **Vinnie Pasquantino** (54.26) and **Kyle Karros** (49.69). **Vinnie Pasquantino** ultimately earned the nod due to a superior platoon advantage against Burns, proving that our optimizer prioritized the dynamic platoon split over the slightly cleaner SP_xERA matchup facing **Kyle Karros**. **Jose Caballero** remains a high-variance play; his raw speed potential is tempered by a negative dynamic platoon adjustment and a difficult matchup against an elite catcher, yet he holds his place to keep our SB volume competitive. \n\nManagers should maintain close surveillance on the **Alex Freeland** situation; despite the #9 spot dragging his score down to 48.87, he remains in the lineup to maximize our daily game cap efficiency. Risks are concentrated in the **Gabriel Moreno** and **Corbin Carroll** slots, both of whom draw Ohtani, though their secondary metrics suggest enough volume to avoid the \"Below Floor\" threshold. We have confirmed that **Trevor Story** and **Mickey Moniak** remain on the IL, leaving no room for further manipulation. With no significant weather threats flagged, we are green-lighted for full output.",
